Cookies Detective — Privacy Policy
Last updated: July 11, 2026

The short version: Cookies Detective does not collect, transmit, or sell any of
your data. Everything the app does happens on your device.

DEVELOPER
Cookies Detective is developed by Dzianis Milasheuski, an individual developer
based in Lithuania. Questions about this policy: info@porconova.com

WHAT WE COLLECT
Nothing. Cookies Detective has no analytics, no ads, no accounts, and no servers
that receive your data. There is no sign-up and no login. We do not know who you
are, which sites you visit, or what cookies you have.

HOW THE APP WORKS
- The Safari extension reads and edits cookies for the site you are viewing,
  using Safari's native cookie API, only while you have the popup open.
- Cookie classification (which company set a cookie, and why) is done entirely
  on your device against a database that ships inside the app. No lookup is ever
  sent to a server — the app never asks anyone "does this user have cookie X?".
- Checkpoints and snapshots you save are stored on your device. If you enable
  iCloud, they sync
  through your own private iCloud account (Apple's Key-Value Storage) to your
  other devices signed in to the same Apple ID; we cannot see them.
- Exported cookie files and audit reports are created on your device and shared
  only where you choose to send them.

WHAT LEAVES YOUR DEVICE
Only what you explicitly export or share, to the destination you pick. Nothing
is sent automatically, and nothing is sent to us.

PERMISSIONS
The "All Websites" permission is required so the extension can read cookies on
the sites you open. Safari describes this as the ability to "see your browsing
history": technically, the extension can read the address of the page you are
viewing when you open the popup. It uses that address solely to show and analyze
that site's cookies, on your device, in the moment — it does not record, store,
or transmit your browsing history anywhere.

PURCHASES
Cookies Detective Pro is sold through Apple's In-App Purchase. Apple, not the
developer, processes payment. We receive no personal or payment information. You
can manage or cancel a subscription in Settings → [Your Name] → Subscriptions on
your device.

YOUR RIGHTS
Because the app collects no personal information on the developer's side, there
is no developer-held data for you to access, correct, export, or delete.
- Data stored on your device can be removed by deleting the app, or by deleting
  individual items inside it.
- Data stored in your iCloud account can be removed by signing the app out of
  iCloud or by deleting it from your iCloud storage in iOS Settings.
- An active subscription can be cancelled in your Apple Account subscriptions.

CHILDREN
Cookies Detective is a developer/privacy utility. It is not directed at children
under the age of 13 and does not knowingly collect any data from children.

REGULATORY NOTES
The app is designed so that no directly identifying personal information (name,
email, IP address, advertising identifier, account ID) is collected by the
developer or by any third party the developer uses. Where Apple acts as a
processor for purchases and iCloud, those activities are governed by Apple's own
privacy policy.

